\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Commit thou all thy griefs
\par And ways into His hands,
\par To His sure truth and tender care,
\par who heaven and earth commands.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Who points the clouds their course.
\par Whom winds and seas obey,
\par He shall direct thy wandering feet,
\par He shall prepare thy way.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thou on the Lord rely,
\par So safe shalt thou go on;
\par Fix on His work thy steadfast eye,
\par So shall thy work be done.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. No profit canst thou gain
\par By self -consuming care:
\par To Him commend thy cause; His ear
\par Attends the softest prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thy everlasting truth ,
\par Father, Thy ceaseless love,
\par Sees all Thy children's wants, and knows 
\par What best for each will prove.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thou everywhere hast sway,
\par And all things  serve Thy might;
\par Thy every act pure blessing is,
\par Thy path unsullied light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. When thou arisest, Lord,
\par What shall Thy work withstand?
\par Whate'ver Thy children want, Thou giv'st
\par And  who shall stay Thy hand?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Give to the winds  thy fears;
\par Hope, and be undismayed:
\par God hears thy sighs, and counts thy tears,
\par God shall lift up thy head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. Through waves, and clouds,and storms
\par He gently clears thy way:
\par Wait thou his time; so shall this night
\par Soon end in joyous day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. Still heavy is thy heart? 
\par Still sink thy spirits down? 
\par Cast off the weigth, let fear depart,
\par Bid every care be gone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11. What though thou rules not?
\par Yet heaven, and earth, and hell
\par Proclaim:  God sitteth on the throne,
\par And ruleth all things well!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 12\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 12. Leave to His sovereign sway
\par To choose and to command;
\par So shall thou wondering own His way.
\par How wise, how strong His hand.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 13\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 13. Far, far above thy thought
\par His counsel shall appear,
\par When fully He the work hath wrought
\par That caused thy needless fear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 14\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 14. Thou seest our weakness, Lord;
\par Our hearts are known to Thee:
\par O lift Thou up the sinkig hand,
\par Confirm the feeble knee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 15\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 15. Let us in life, in death,
\par Thy steadfast tuth declare,
\par And publish with our latest braeth
\par Thy love and guardian care. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

